CBDT Circular No. 03/2023 dated 28th March 2023 (F.No. 370142/14/2022-TPL) issued under Section 119 read with Rule 114AAA of the Income-tax Rules, 1962 and Section 234H of the Income-tax Act, 1961.

1. Reactivation Timeline: As per Para 4 of Circular 03/2023 and Rule 114AAA, an inoperative PAN can be made operative again within thirty (30) days from the date of intimation of Aadhaar to the prescribed authority after payment of the prescribed fee of Rs. 1,000 under Section 234H. Once the late fee of ₹1,000 is paid on the e-filing portal via e-Pay Tax (Major Head 0021, Minor Head 500), the taxpayer must submit the linking request under 'Link Aadhaar'. The PAN becomes operative within 30 days from the date of submission of the linking request.

2. Statutory Consequences During Inoperative Period:
(a) No refund of any amount of tax or part thereof due under the Act shall be made to the taxpayer;
(b) No interest shall be payable on such refund for the period during which the PAN remained inoperative;
(c) Where tax is deductible at source (TDS) under Chapter XVII-B, tax shall be deducted at higher rate in accordance with Section 206AA (flat 20% on salary and payments);
(d) Where tax is collectible at source (TCS) under Chapter XVII-BB, tax shall be collected at higher rate in accordance with Section 206CC.
